e it is over 60,000 ticks (1.3c), and the clock it does print (1.6d). **The suite never claims it compared the text.** The manual recipe — which pawn, which tab, which number, and the ticks→hours conversion — is a numbered section of the `.md` |\n| replay Captain's four reads from `RUNS/m1-20260831/` | **NOT DECIDABLE**, as comment #2 already says. The transcript records the OUTPUT of a pawn state, not the state; the run left no save; the pawn does not exist. Phase 2 builds his SHAPE — 20+ bleeding injuries plus `BloodLoss` at 0.478, the severity the post-mortem back-solved — and says it is a reconstruction in the suite's own docstring AND in a `note(\"2.0\")` that prints on every run. It is not called a replay anywhere |\n\n**Not reachable at all, and said rather than skipped:** the `coma` outcome and the `(Deathless)` branch of the widget. Both need a Biotech pawn carrying the Deathless gene and there is no `dev:` verb that adds a gene — so the pawn on which `outcome` and `game_shows_clock` deliberately DISAGREE (Deathless with a destroyed brain) is unstageable. `deathless_gene` is asserted false throughout, so the branch is unexercised rather than silently assumed, and 9.4h exercises the python side offline.\n\n## SUITE versus YOUR MANUAL PASS, because they are not the same thing\n\nComment #3 measured five of these by hand and banked the envelopes. **Nothing below is claimed as new.** The distinction that matters is that a bullet proved by hand is not a bullet that can be re-proved on demand, and the suite is the deliverable.\n\n| already measured and banked by you (#3) | what the SUITE adds |\n|---|---|\n| `BloodLoss` at row 0 with **34 dropped** (54 hediffs, cap 20), read `09` | **stages it live** (phase 2 damages a pawn past the cap, then adds BloodLoss at 0.478) AND **re-asserts your envelope offline** at 9.5a-9.5c, so the claim survives without a bench |\n| `life_threatening` **false at 0.562 / true at 0.623**, reads `09`/`11` | 9.5d/9.5e assert both sides 